build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:6:source-management. It is the implementation blueprint for source attachment\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:17:- Epic: `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md`\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:18:- Test plan: `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/test-plan.md`\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:31:attachment beyond the Epic 5-7 sequence.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:37:| Process-scoped shadowing needs exact read rule | Tech Design Question 7 | Design defines an active-source resolver that combines project-scoped and process-scoped attachments, shadows by `repositoryFullName + targetRef`, and excludes detached rows. | Resolved |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:50:| 2 | What exact durable schema should represent source attachments and provenance visibility? | Extend `sourceAttachments` with `repositoryFullName`, freshness fields, refresh progress fields, and soft-detach fields. Add `sourceProvenance` for process-specific provenance with copied immutable source identity. Artifact ownership remains untouched. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:51:| 3 | What exact conflict rule applies for same repository/target ref across related contexts? | Duplicate key is active `projectId + processId + repositoryFullName + targetRef`. Same identity/ref may exist once at project scope and once at process scope. Process-scoped rows shadow project-scoped rows only for that process's current-source read. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:53:| 5 | What provenance surface shows informed-work and received-code-update relationships? | Add a process provenance endpoint and client section that reads durable `sourceProvenance` entries. Entries are `informed_work` or `received_code_update`, copy repository identity, and enrich current attachment context independently when available. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:56:| 8 | What soft-detach representation preserves identity and provenance? | Add `detachedAt` and `detachedByUserId` to source attachments. Active listings filter detached rows, but provenance entries remain durable because they copy identity and may retain nullable `sourceAttachmentId`. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:61:already made source attachments visible enough for hydration and checkpointing,\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:79:provenance intent. Convex stores durable source attachment and provenance rows\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:85:those provenance records without asking source attachments to become archive\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:94:| Projects | Core architecture | Project-scoped source attachments appear in the project shell and can be managed there |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:95:| Processes | Core architecture | Process-scoped attachments, current-source views, and source provenance appear in the process work surface |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:96:| Sources | Core architecture | Primary Epic 6 domain; owns repository attachment lifecycle, freshness, detach, and provenance records |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:97:| Environments | Core architecture | Hydrates active source attachments and reports freshness/checkpoint effects |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:136:| GitHub API / clone identity | Validate repository existence, access, canonical `owner/name`, and target ref resolution | Mock in server service tests through a `GitHubRepositoryResolver` interface |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:138:| Convex | Durable source attachment and provenance persistence | Use Convex function tests for durable invariants; in Fastify service tests use existing PlatformStore fakes or in-memory harnesses |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:158:| Process-scoped attach updates current process source refs immediately | The epic says a process-scoped attachment belongs to one process as current source state and becomes visible immediately | `attachProcessSource` persists the source row and adds its id to that process's current source refs in the same orchestration path |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:160:| Read-write attachments require branch-like target refs | Durable code updates need a writable moving ref rather than an immutable commit/tag | `read_write` attachments reject tag/commit target refs; `read_only` attachments may use branch/tag/commit |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:161:| Provenance records copy immutable identity | Detach or access loss must not erase process history | Provenance stores `repositoryFullName`, `repositoryUrl`, `targetRef`, relationship kind, and optional attachment id |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-an