and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:692:      - \"tests/service/client/source-attachment-section.test.ts\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:701:        evidence: \"The story scope explicitly includes a project-scoped attach UI action and a process-scoped attach UI action, and AC-1.1 expects the user to attach while viewing the project shell or process work surface (docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process.md:24-25,49-58). The project shell still renders only the existing Create process button plus passive sections (apps/platform/client/features/projects/project-shell-page.ts:71-99), the source attachment section is read-only markup with no form/button/callback (apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-section.ts:24-69), and the process work surface only renders existing controls/materials/history/side-work with no attach affordance or handler (apps/platform/client/features/processes/process-work-surface-page.ts:183-221). No client module calls the new POST /api/projects/:projectId/source-attachments or /api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/source-attachments routes, so a user cannot complete TC-1.1a or TC-1.1b from the required UI surfaces.\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:704:          - \"apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-section.ts\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:716:        evidence: \"AC-1.2 requires the new attachment's repository identity and chosen scope to be visible immediately after creation (docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process.md:29-30,60-65). The process-surface contract cannot carry that data: ProcessSourceReference omits repositoryFullName and attachmentScope (apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts:318-330), the materials reader only projects displayName/purpose/accessMode/repositoryUrl/targetRef/hydrationState/updatedAt into currentSources (apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts:90-99), and the process materials UI renders purpose/access/hydration/target ref/updated only (apps/platform/client/features/processes/process-materials-section.ts:220-253). The process attach API test likewise asserts only displayName and targetRef in materials.currentSources (tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts:223-234), while the lone TC-1.2 client test only covers the project shell source section (tests/service/client/source-attachment-section.test.ts:13-31).\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:732:        evidence: \"The story scope explicitly includes a project-scoped attach UI action and a process-scoped attach UI action, and AC-1.1 expects the user to attach while viewing the project shell or process work surface (docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process.md:24-25,49-58). The project shell still renders only the existing Create process button plus passive sections (apps/platform/client/features/projects/project-shell-page.ts:71-99), the source attachment section is read-only markup with no form/button/callback (apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-section.ts:24-69), and the process work surface only renders existing controls/materials/history/side-work with no attach affordance or handler (apps/platform/client/features/processes/process-work-surface-page.ts:183-221). No client module calls the new POST /api/projects/:projectId/source-attachments or /api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/source-attachments routes, so a user cannot complete TC-1.1a or TC-1.1b from the required UI surfaces.\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:735:          - \"apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-section.ts\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:747:        evidence: \"AC-1.2 requires the new attachment's repository identity and chosen scope to be visible immediately after creation (docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process.md:29-30,60-65). The process-surface contract cannot carry that data: ProcessSourceReference omits repositoryFullName and attachmentScope (apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts:318-330), the materials reader only projects displayName/purpose/accessMode/repositoryUrl/targetRef/hydrationState/updatedAt into currentSources (apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts:90-99), and the process materials UI renders purpose/access/hydration/target ref/updated only (apps/platform/client/features/processes/process-materials-section.ts:220-253). The process attach API test likewise asserts only displayName and targetRef in materials.currentSources (tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts:223-234), while the lone TC-1.2 client test only covers the project shell source section (tests/service/client/source-attachment-section.test.ts:13-31).\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:775:        command: \"corepack pnpm vitest run tests/service/server/source-management-service.test.ts tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts tests/service/client/source-attachment-section.test.ts convex/sourceAttachments.test.ts\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:785:      - \"materials.currentSources omits repositoryFullName and attachmentScope, so a process-scoped attach cannot satisfy the required identity/scope visibility on the live process surface.\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:800:      path: \"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process/004-verify.json\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:810:Path: /Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process/story-lead/001-current.json\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:825:    path: \"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/