argetRef: 'feature/story-2',\n   404\t      hydrationState: 'not_hydrated',\n   405\t    });\n   406\t\n   407\t    const [updatedAttachment] = await platformStore.listProjectSourceAttachments({\n   408\t      projectId: projectSummary.projectId,\n   409\t    });\n   410\t    expect(updatedAttachment).toMatchObject({\n   411\t      sourceAttachmentId: createdAttachment.sourceAttachmentId,\n   412\t      purpose: 'review',\n   413\t      accessMode: 'read_write',\n   414\t      targetRef: 'feature/story-2',\n   415\t    });\n   416\t\n   417\t    await app.close();\n   418\t  });\n   419\t});\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_70","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/02-manage-purpose-access-mode-and-target-ref.md | sed -n '30,140p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_70","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/02-manage-purpose-access-mode-and-target-ref.md | sed -n '30,140p'\"","aggregated_output":"    30\t\n    31\t- Initial attach behavior\n    32\t- Refresh execution\n    33\t- Provenance recording\n    34\t- Detach behavior\n    35\t\n    36\t**Dependencies**\n    37\t\n    38\t- Story 1 attach behavior\n    39\t- Story 0 shared contracts\n    40\t- [tech-design.md](../tech-design.md) Flow 2\n    41\t- [test-plan.md](../test-plan.md) Chunk 2 tests\n    42\t\n    43\t### Acceptance Criteria\n    44\t<!-- Jira: Acceptance Criteria field -->\n    45\t**AC-2.1:** Each source attachment records purpose, access mode, and target ref as durable source metadata.\n    46\t\n    47\t- **TC-2.1a: Purpose, access mode, and target ref visible**\n    48\t  - Given: A source attachment exists\n    49\t  - When: The source attachment appears in the current surface\n    50\t  - Then: The purpose, access mode, and target ref are visible\n    51\t\n    52\t**AC-2.2:** The user can update purpose, access mode, and target ref for an existing source attachment.\n    53\t\n    54\t- **TC-2.2a: Update source metadata**\n    55\t  - Given: A source attachment exists\n    56\t  - When: User updates purpose, access mode, or target ref\n    57\t  - Then: The source attachment stores and displays the updated metadata\n    58\t\n    59\t**AC-2.3:** Access mode clearly distinguishes read-only and writable source attachments.\n    60\t\n    61\t- **TC-2.3a: Read-only attachment is identifiable**\n    62\t  - Given: A source attachment has read-only access mode\n    63\t  - When: The source attachment appears in the current surface\n    64\t  - Then: The user can tell that the source attachment is read-only\n    65\t- **TC-2.3b: Writable attachment is identifiable**\n    66\t  - Given: A source attachment has writable access mode\n    67\t  - When: The source attachment appears in the current surface\n    68\t  - Then: The user can tell that the source attachment is writable\n    69\t\n    70\t**AC-2.4:** Updating the target ref updates freshness state when the current hydrated working copy no longer matches the attached source definition.\n    71\t\n    72\t- **TC-2.4a: Target-ref change marks source stale**\n    73\t  - Given: A source attachment was previously hydrated\n    74\t  - When: User changes its target ref\n    75\t  - Then: The source attachment no longer appears current and indicates that rehydration is required\n    76\t\n    77\t### Technical Design\n    78\t<!-- Jira: Technical Notes or sub-section of Description -->\n    79\t#### Architecture Context\n    80\t\n    81\tThis story updates durable source metadata without changing canonical source\n    82\tidentity. Fastify owns update validation and writable-ref policy, while Convex\n    83\tpersists the update atomically. The critical behavior is that a target-ref\n    84\tchange can invalidate the previously hydrated working copy and must carry a\n    85\tfreshness transition in the same durable write.\n    86\t\n    87\t#### Route\n    88\t\n    89\t| Operation | Method | Path | Service Method |\n    90\t|---|---|---|---|\n    91\t| Update source | `PATCH` | `/api/projects/:projectId/source-attachments/:sourceAttachmentId` | `updateSource` |\n    92\t\n    93\t#### Update Request\n    94\t\n    95\t| Field | Type | Required | Validation |\n    96\t|---|---|---|---|\n    97\t| `purpose` | enum | no | `research`, `review`, `implementation`, `other` |\n    98\t| `accessMode` | enum | no | `read_only`, `read_write` |\n    99\t| `targetRef` | string/null | no | non-empty when present |\n   100\t\n   101\t#### Update Response\n   102\t\n   103\t| Field | Type | Required | Description |\n   104\t|---|---|---|---|\n   105\t| `sourceAttachment` | Source Attachment Summary | yes | Updated durable source attachment state |\n   106\t\n   107\t#### Service Responsibilities\n   108\t\n   109\t- Load and update by `sourceAttachmentId` regardless of whether the source is project-scoped or process-scoped.\n   110\t- Validate authenticated project access and source membership in the project.\n   111\t- Preserve source identity fields unless an explicit future story changes identity behavior.\n   112\t- Normalize target ref before persistence.\n   113\t- If `targetRef` changes while `hydrationState === 'hydrated'`, persist `hydrationState: 'stale'` and a freshness reason such as `target_ref_changed`.\n   114\t- Enforce writable-ref policy for `read_write` attachments.\n   115\t\n   116\t#### Client Responsibilities\n   117\t\n   118\t- Render purpose, access mode, target ref, and updated freshness state as readable text.\n   119\t- Distinguish `read_only` and `read_write` without relying on color alone.\n   120\t- Update the current source row in place after a successful PATCH response.\n   121\t\n   122\t#### Implementation Targets\n   123\t\n   124\t| Area | Files / Modules |\n   125\t|------|-----------------|\n   126\t| Update route and schema | `apps/platform/server/routes/source-management.ts`, `apps/platform/server/schemas/source-management.ts` |\n   127\t| Metadata update logic | `apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-management.service.ts` |\n   128\t| Durable source update | `apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts`, `convex/sourceAttachments.ts` |\n   129\t| Project/process source rendering | `apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-section.ts`, `apps/platform/client/features/processes/process-materials-section.ts` |\n   130\t\n   131\t#### Design References\n   132\t\n   133\t- [tech-design.md](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:331), lines 331-380\n   134\t- [tech-design.md](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:555), lines 555-572\n   135\t- [test-plan.md](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/test-plan.md:45), lines 45-49\n   136\t\n   137\t#### Test Mapping\n   138\t\n   139\t| TC | Test File / Check | Test Description |\n   140\t|----|-------------------|------------------|\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
